<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Innioasis Notice Feed Specification  ·  notice.xml
  Canonical URL: https://innioasis.app/notice.xml
  (The plural file name notices.xml is not used. Every client, the app and the
  website, reads this one feed.)

  One feed drives two kinds of presentation:

    CONTEXTUAL (one notice at a time)
      · Updater CE main window notice card / toast
      · innioasis.app software list (firmware.html, above the release table)
      Shows exactly one notice at a time and rotates through the notices that
      apply to the viewer, so every relevant notice can be read without
      expanding anything or opening the Notices view.

    UNFILTERED (every current notice)
      · Updater CE Notices tab / full list
      · innioasis.app bell tray
      · innioasis.app notices.html
      Always lists every current notice, to everyone, whatever the targeting.

  ROOT
    <notices updated="YYYY-MM-DD"> … </notices>
    updated is advisory metadata for humans and caches. Clients re-fetch the
    feed on every launch, so no cache-busting value is required.

  A NOTICE
    <notice …attributes…>
      <title>        required, the headline.
      <content>      required, one or two sentences (aliases: <summary>, <body>)
      <full_content> optional Markdown body; falls back to <content>.
      <url>          optional page for the notice (alias <link>). A URL that is
                     only the bare site root is ignored; the notice then links
                     to its own page (notices.html?notice=<id>).
    </notice>

  IDENTITY AND LIFECYCLE
    id          required. Stable and unique. Convention: YYYY-MM-DD-slug.
    from        optional ISO date YYYY-MM-DD; visible on or after this day.
    until       optional ISO date YYYY-MM-DD; visible up to and including it.
    persistent  "true" | "false" (default "false").
                  false: dismissing it is remembered, so it does not return.
                  true: returns on every launch even if dismissed before.
                  Any change to the feed's contents re-shows it either way.
    severity    "info" | "warning" | "critical" (default "info"). Drives colour
                and contextual ordering; critical and warning rank above info.

  TARGETING
    All four attributes are optional. Each takes a comma-separated list,
    case-insensitive, with "*" meaning any. Attribute names match the app and
    slidia_manifest.xml so the same notice can be written once for both.

    models            Device models, e.g. "Y1" or "Y1,Y2". Matches the app's
                      Device Model selector and slidia_manifest.xml device=.
    device_type       Hardware revision, e.g. "A" or "A,B" (Y1 Type A / Type B).
                      Matches the app's Device Type selector and a device whose
                      type the app has logged. Has no effect on a model that
                      has no revisions.
    firmware_repo     "owner/repo" exactly as repo= in slidia_manifest.xml,
                      e.g. "rockbox-y1/rockbox". Comma-separate for several.
                      This is what makes a notice appear when someone selects
                      the software built from that repository.
    firmware_version  Release tag or version, e.g. "3.1.2", "v3.1.2", "3.1.*".
                      "*" is a wildcard; a leading "v" and letter case are
                      ignored. Matches the release the viewer has installed,
                      has selected, or is currently looking at.

    EXAMPLES
      <notice id="…" models="Y2" device_type="A" severity="warning">
      <notice id="…" models="Y1,Y2" firmware_repo="rockbox-y1/rockbox">
      <notice id="…" firmware_repo="spycemagic/y2-rockbox"
              firmware_version="3.1.*" severity="critical">
      <notice id="…">            ← broadcast: no targeting attributes at all

  MATCHING RULE  (every client implements exactly this)
    A notice is a BROADCAST notice when it declares none of the four targeting
    attributes. It is relevant to everyone, everywhere, always.

    A notice is a TARGETED notice when it declares at least one of them. It is
    ELIGIBLE for a viewer only when it is inside its date window and, for every
    targeting attribute it declares, the viewer's context has a known value
    that matches. Attributes a notice does not declare never filter it.

    Fail closed: if the viewer's context does not know a dimension the notice
    declares (for example firmware_version before any release is known), the
    notice is not eligible for the contextual slot. It still appears in the
    unfiltered views, where its targets are shown as plain labels.

  VIEWER CONTEXT
    model             the selected Device Model, and in Updater CE also the
                      model it logged for update reminders. Both count.
    device_type       the selected or logged hardware revision.
    firmware_repo     repo of the selected or installed software.
    firmware_version  tag of the release installed, selected, or shown.
    A context dimension is only ever "known" from a real app or website state;
    it is never guessed. Model is known from the selector. Device type is known
    for Y1. Repo is known once a software project is selected. Version is known
    once a release is loaded or selected.

  CONTEXTUAL CARD
    · exactly ONE notice is visible at a time
    · the card rotates through the whole eligible set (broadcast + targeted)
      so the visitor sees every relevant notice without expanding anything
    · ordering: a notice that just became eligible goes first (for example the
      Y2 notices right after the visitor selects Y2), then severity
      critical > warning > info, then newest from=, then id
    · a context change re-ranks immediately; the rotation timer restarts
    · rotation pauses while a pointer or keyboard focus is inside the card and
      is disabled under prefers-reduced-motion, where the dot controls remain
    · dismissal hides that notice for the current run only; the card continues
      with the next eligible notice
-->
<notices updated="2026-11-03">

  <notice id="2026-11-03-rockbox-y2-warn" persistent="false" severity="warning" from="2026-11-03" until="2026-12-31" models="Y2" firmware_repo="spycemagic/y2-rockbox">
    <title>Users having issues with Rockbox for Y2.</title>
    <content>Rockbox 360p themes not working and music not reading from MicroSD.</content>
    <full_content>Rockbox for Y2 has two open problems reported by the community:

- **360p themes do not apply.** The player keeps showing the stock 360p artwork.
- **Music on a MicroSD card is not listed** after a Rockbox install.

If you rely on a MicroSD library, stay on Original Software until these are fixed.

> Restoring the original firmware takes one run of Updater CE. Music on your MicroSD card is left alone, but music saved to the Y2's internal storage is erased: on Y2 the Keep Data option in Updater CE 2.5.1 only carries data across between firmwares that are cross-compatible, and moving to Original Software is not one of those cases.

The steps are in the [Y2 stock restore guide](https://innioasis.app/guides/restore-original-y2.html).</full_content>
    <url>https://innioasis.app</url>
  </notice>

  <notice id="2026-10-25-firmware-advisory" persistent="false" severity="info" from="2026-10-25" until="2026-12-31">
    <title>About Notices in Updater CE</title>
    <content>You'll get important alerts about device safety issues reported by the community here, such as when devices are being bricked by certain firmware.</content>
    <full_content>Notices are how the community warns about device safety issues, firmware that should not be installed on a particular hardware revision, and new software releases.

- **Each notice has its own page** on this site, so a warning can be read in full instead of being cut down to one line.
- **The app and the software list show one notice at a time**, rotating through the ones that apply to the player you selected.
- **This one is for everyone.** A notice without a target applies wherever notices are shown.
- **A notice without a specific page** simply opens its own page here; a link to the bare site root is ignored.

Use the bell in the header to see every current notice at any time.</full_content>
    <link>https://innioasis.app</link>
  </notice>

</notices>
